# environment.env.template
#
# Reference template for Claude Code web environment variables.
# Paste relevant lines into: Claude Code web > environment settings > Environment variables.
# Format: KEY=value, one pair per line, NO quotes (quotes become part of the value).
# Changes take effect on the NEXT session/container, not the running one.
#
# WARNING: environment config is visible to anyone who can edit the environment,
# and there is no secrets store. NEVER put a PAT, API key, or password in THIS
# committed template file - it lives in the repo (Imperative 1 +
# claude-sp-guards.md section 3.1).
#
# PAT for git auth: setting GITHUB_PAT in the Claude Code web environment
# settings panel (NOT this file) is acceptable, provided it is a short-lived,
# repo-scoped, minimum-permission fine-grained PAT and the environment is not
# shared. Human user manages its secrecy when injecting it via the Claude Code
# web UI, and rotates on expiry. The panel value is injected as a runtime env
# var and does not enter the session transcript. See claude-code-agent.md
# Imperative 5.
#
# --- optional tuning (uncomment + set as needed) ---
#
# Compact context earlier than the ~95% default. Aligns with the prompteng
# token-budget thresholds (20% / 15% remaining).
# CLAUDE_AUTOCOMPACT_PCT_OVERRIDE=80
#
# --- platform-managed: do NOT set these yourself ---
# CLAUDE_CODE_REMOTE             set to true by the platform in cloud sessions
# CLAUDE_CODE_REMOTE_SESSION_ID  cloud session id, read-only
